DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nTopics: Law\nDetails: https://www.law.cam.ac.uk
 /events/cambridge-family-law-cfl-hybrid-seminar-justifying-relational-obli
 gations-beyond-autonomy\nSign-up only to join online: https://cam-ac-uk.zo
 om.us/webinar/register/WN_5oagNLNCQJqnj8BVq_sCbw\nDate/time: \n\n Tuesday 
 24 November 2026 \n\n 12:00pm to 1:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Faculty of Law\
 , David Williams Building\n\n B16\n\n About \n\n Speaker: Dr Matt Hasler (
 Teaching By-Fellow in Law and Philosophy\, Churchill College)\n Family law
  systems characteristically impose relational obligations: legal duties of
  financial provision that attach to personal or familial relationships\, a
 nd thereby impose special financial responsibilities on their bearers. Rel
 ational obligations pose a host of important normative questions. To which
  kinds of relationships should they attach? What should their content be? 
 And to what extent\, if at all\, should parties be entitled to alter or di
 sapply such obligations by means of private contracts?\n It is often sugge
 sted that our answers to these questions will be significantly determined 
 by our attitudes to two apparently competing principles. On the one hand\,
  respect f
END:VEVENT
